# Shatter — Controls

Shatter is played on the keyboard alone. This file defines every action the game
answers to and the keys bound to it. What the ship does when it turns, thrusts,
and fires is in `specs/ship.md` and `specs/weapons.md`, and the screens the menu
actions move between are in `specs/ui.md`.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
## How input reaches the game

This game stands on no engine, so the keyboard belongs to the runtime layer you
write. It listens to the page and reports which keys are down, by their
`KeyboardEvent.code` values, along with the press edge of each. Every key below is
named by its `code`, so a binding is a physical key rather than a
layout-dependent character.

## The keys

| Key | While playing | On a menu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ArrowUp`, `KeyW` | Thrust | Move the selection up |
| `ArrowDown`, `KeyS` | — | Move the selection down |
| `ArrowLeft`, `KeyA` | Rotate counter-clockwise | — |
| `ArrowRight`, `KeyD` | Rotate clockwise | — |
| `Space` | Fire the gun | Confirm the selection |
| `Enter` | — | Confirm the selection |
{{#if (eq variant.slug "warhead")}}
| `KeyF` | Launch the torpedo | — |
{{/if}}
| `KeyP` | Pause | — |
| `Escape` | Pause | Leave the screen |
| `KeyM` | Toggle sound | Toggle sound |

`Space` fires while the game is being played and confirms on a screen showing a
menu, and `Escape` pauses while the game is being played and leaves the screen
otherwise. The screen decides which meaning applies.
{{else}}
## How input reaches the game

Input reaches the game as named actions from the {{engine.name}} engine, which
documents them in the `engine/` directory at the root of this repository. The game
registers the layout `LAYOUT` (`dpad-4-two-buttons`), which carries four-way
movement and two buttons, and registers every action in `ACTIONS` against the keys
`BINDINGS` gives it. `BINDINGS` names each key by its `KeyboardEvent.code`, so a
binding is a physical key rather than a layout-dependent character.

The whole of `ACTIONS` is registered.

## The actions

| Action | While playing | On a menu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `up` | Thrust | Move the selection up |
| `down` | — | Move the selection down |
| `left` | Rotate counter-clockwise | — |
| `right` | Rotate clockwise | — |
| `a` | Fire the gun | — |
{{#if (eq variant.slug "warhead")}}
| `b` | Launch the torpedo | — |
{{else}}
| `b` | Fire the gun | — |
{{/if}}
| `confirm` | — | Confirm the selection |
| `back` | Pause | Leave the screen |
| `pause` | Pause | — |
| `mute` | Toggle sound | Toggle sound |

## The bindings

| Action | Keys |
| --- | --- |
| `up` | `ArrowUp`, `KeyW` |
| `down` | `ArrowDown`, `KeyS` |
| `left` | `ArrowLeft`, `KeyA` |
| `right` | `ArrowRight`, `KeyD` |
| `a` | `Space` |
{{#if (eq variant.slug "warhead")}}
| `b` | `KeyF` |
{{else}}
| `b` | `Space` |
{{/if}}
| `confirm` | `Enter`, `Space` |
| `back` | `Escape` |
| `pause` | `KeyP`, `Escape` |
| `mute` | `KeyM` |

`Escape` drives both `back` and `pause`, and the screen decides which one applies:
it pauses while the game is being played and leaves the screen otherwise. `Space`
likewise drives firing while the game is being played and confirms on a screen
showing a menu.
{{/if}}

## Holds and presses

Rotation and thrust are read as holds: the ship turns and accelerates for as long
as the key is down and stops the moment it is released.

Firing is read as a press and as a hold. One press takes one shot; holding the key
takes a shot at the gun's own gate, as `specs/weapons.md` states.
{{#if (eq variant.slug "warhead")}}
The torpedo is read as a press alone: one launch per press, with no repeat while
the key is held.
{{/if}}

Confirming, leaving a screen, pausing, and muting are read as press edges, once
per press.

## Menus

Every menu is vertical. The up and down inputs move the highlight by one entry and
wrap at both ends, so moving down from the last entry highlights the first and
moving up from the first highlights the last. The highlight is therefore always on
one of the menu's own entries. Confirming takes the highlighted entry, and
`specs/ui.md` states each screen's entries and where each leads.

## The debug overlay

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
The read-only debug overlay `specs/instrumentation.md` describes is shown and
hidden by the backtick key, `KeyboardEvent.code` `Backquote`. It is off when the
game starts. The overlay and its toggle are part of the runtime layer you write.
{{else}}
The read-only debug overlay is the engine's, shown and hidden by the backtick key,
`KeyboardEvent.code` `Backquote`, and off when the game starts. It is not one of
Shatter's actions. What it shows is in `specs/instrumentation.md`.
{{/if}}
